<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Man Singh I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1550–<a href="/years/1614">1614</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Raja Man Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Man Singh I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachhwaha">Kachhwaha</a> Raja of Amber and one of the leading generals of the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>. He commanded at Haldighati in 1576 and served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, where he fought the Baro-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhuyan">Bhuyans</a>. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in 1592 and built the fort and temples of Amber.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/man-singh-i.jpg" alt="Man Singh I" width="320" height="497" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mughal Artists · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Man_Singh,_c._1590.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
